{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"bd1411da-6b20-4ef0-ba7a-9ba3623aa276","ts":"2026-07-16T10:45:20.018-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"58","nodeName":"Google Gemini Chat Model","workflowName":"ForgeAI - Software Architect Agent","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","workflowId":"GtMVKU0V13n1DZOO","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are the Software Architect Agent of ForgeAI.\\n\\nYou are a Senior Software Architect with 15+ years of experience.\\n\\nYou never write implementation code.\\n\\nYou receive the outputs from the Planner Agent and Research Agent.\\n\\nYour responsibility is to design the complete technical architecture.\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"architecture_type\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"backend_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"database_design\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"api_design\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"microservices\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"authentication\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"deployment_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"scalability_plan\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"security_considerations\\\":[\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\nReturn only JSON.\\n\\nDo not explain anything.\\n\\nDo not use markdown.\\nHuman: ={}\"],\"options\":{\"google_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"]},\"base_url\":\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com\",\"model\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\",\"temperature\":0.2},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"architecture_type\\\": \\\"Client-Server with Microservices\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend_architecture\\\": \\\"Single Page Application (SPA) using React.js with TypeScript, bundled with Webpack/Vite. State management handled by Redux Toolkit or React Query. Styling with Tailwind CSS or Styled Components.\\\",\\n  \\\"backend_architecture\\\": \\\"Microservices architecture, each service developed using Node.js with Express.js or Fastify, or Python with FastAPI. Services communicate via RESTful APIs or asynchronous messaging (e.g., Kafka/RabbitMQ). API Gateway handles request routing, authentication, and rate limiting.\\\",\\n  \\\"database_design\\\": {\\n    \\\"primary_database\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Relational data storage for core business entities (e.g., Users, Products, Orders, Transactions). Chosen for its ACID compliance, strong consistency, and robust feature set.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"secondary_database\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"MongoDB\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"NoSQL document database for flexible schema data (e.g., User Activity Logs, Notifications, Analytics Data). Chosen for its scalability and flexibility with unstructured data.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"caching_layer\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"Redis\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"In-memory data store for caching frequently accessed data, session management, and real-time data processing. Chosen for its high performance and versatility.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"api_design\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Public API Gateway\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"RESTful API\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Entry point for all client requests. Handles request routing to appropriate microservices, authentication, authorization, rate limiting, and potentially caching. Implemented using technologies like AWS API Gateway, Nginx, or Kong.\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints_example\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/v1/users\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/v1/products/{id}\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/v1/orders\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"data_format\\\": \\\"JSON\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Internal Microservice APIs\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"RESTful API / Message Queues\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"APIs for inter-service communication. Primarily RESTful for synchronous calls, with message queues (e.g., Kafka, RabbitMQ) for asynchronous events and task processing to ensure loose coupling and resilience.\\\",\\n      \\\"data_format\\\": \\\"JSON / Avro (for message queues)\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\": [\\n    \\\"/src\\\",\\n    \\\"  /frontend\\\",\\n    \\\"    /public\\\",\\n    \\\"    /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /components\\\",\\n    \\\"      /pages\\\",\\n    \\\"      /services\\\",\\n    \\\"      /store\\\",\\n    \\\"      /utils\\\",\\n    \\\"      /App.tsx\\\",\\n    \\\"      /index.tsx\\\",\\n    \\\"  /backend\\\",\\n    \\\"    /api-gateway\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"    /user-service\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"        /controllers\\\",\\n    \\\"        /models\\\",\\n    \\\"        /routes\\\",\\n    \\\"        /services\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"      /tests\\\",\\n    \\\"    /product-service\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"    /order-service\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"    /payment-service\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"    /notification-service\\\",\\n    \\\"      /src\\\",\\n    \\\"      /config\\\",\\n    \\\"  /shared\\\",\\n    \\\"    /types\\\",\\n    \\\"    /utils\\\",\\n    \\\"/config\\\",\\n    \\\"/docs\\\",\\n    \\\"/infra\\\",\\n    \\\"  /kubernetes\\\",\\n    \\\"  /terraform\\\",\\n    \\\"/tests\\\",\\n    \\\"/scripts\\\",\\n    \\\"/docker-compose.yml\\\",\\n    \\\"/package.json\\\",\\n    \\\"/README.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"microservices\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"API Gateway Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Routes external requests, handles authentication, authorization, rate limiting, and load balancing to internal services.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"User Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Manages user authentication (registration, login, password reset), user profiles, and authorization roles.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Product Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Manages product catalog, inventory, pricing, and product search functionality.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Handles order creation, management, status updates, and order history.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Payment Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Integrates with third-party payment gateways, processes payments, and manages refunds.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Notification Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Sends email, SMS, and push notifications to users based on system events.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Analytics Service\\\",\\n      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Collects and processes user behavior data, generates reports and insights.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"authentication\\\": \\\"OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect for user authentication (e.g., Google, GitHub, or custom identity provider). JWT (JSON Web Tokens) for stateless session management. The API Gateway validates JWTs for every incoming request and passes user context to downstream services. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) implemented at the service level.\\\",\\n  \\\"deployment_architecture\\\": \\\"Cloud-native deployment on AWS (or GCP/Azure). Services are containerized using Docker and orchestrated with Kubernetes (EKS). CI/CD pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) automate builds, tests, and deployments. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform manages cloud resources. Load balancers (e.g., AWS ALB) distribute traffic. CDN (e.g., AWS CloudFront) for static assets. Centralized logging (e.g., ELK Stack, AWS CloudWatch Logs) and monitoring (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, AWS CloudWatch Metrics).\\\",\\n  \\\"scalability_plan\\\": \\\"Horizontal scaling for all stateless microservices by adding more instances based on load. Database replication (read replicas) and sharding for PostgreSQL. Caching with Redis to reduce database load. Asynchronous communication via message queues (Kafka) to decouple services and handle high throughput. CDN for global distribution of static content. Auto-scaling groups for Kubernetes pods and underlying EC2 instances. Load balancing across multiple availability zones.\\\",\\n  \\\"security_considerations\\\": [\\n    \\\"OWASP Top 10 adherence for all web applications and APIs.\\\",\\n    \\\"HTTPS/TLS encryption for all communication (in-transit and at-rest).\\\",\\n    \\\"Input validation and sanitization to prevent injection attacks (SQL, XSS, etc.).\\\",\\n    \\\"Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) with the principle of least privilege.\\\",\\n    \\\"Rate limiting and throttling on API Gateway to prevent abuse and DDoS attacks.\\\",\\n    \\\"Secure secrets management (e.g., AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault) for API keys, database credentials.\\\",\\n    \\\"Regular security audits, vulnerability scanning, and penetration testing.\\\",\\n    \\\"Web Application Firewall (WAF) to protect against common web exploits.\\\",\\n    \\\"Centralized logging and monitoring for security events and anomalies.\\\",\\n    \\\"Data encryption at rest for all databases and storage.\\\",\\n    \\\"Strict network segmentation and firewall rules between microservices and external access.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":1671,\"promptTokens\":175,\"totalTokens\":1846}}}"}}
