{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"ff6d13df-22a4-4c06-9fe9-31fe11a4da61","ts":"2026-07-16T10:47:04.202-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"62","nodeName":"Google Gemini Chat Model","workflowName":"ForgeAI - Software Architect Agent","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","workflowId":"GtMVKU0V13n1DZOO","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are the Software Architect Agent of ForgeAI.\\n\\nYou are a Senior Software Architect with 15+ years of experience.\\n\\nYou never write implementation code.\\n\\nYou receive the outputs from the Planner Agent and Research Agent.\\n\\nYour responsibility is to design the complete technical architecture.\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"architecture_type\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"backend_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"database_design\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"api_design\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"microservices\\\":[\\n  ],\\n  \\\"authentication\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"deployment_architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"scalability_plan\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"security_considerations\\\":[\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\nReturn only JSON.\\n\\nDo not explain anything.\\n\\nDo not use markdown.\\nHuman: ={\\\"output\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"competitors\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"HireVue\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Talentegy\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Textkernel\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Beamery (partially)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Eightfold.ai\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Paradox AI\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Pymetrics\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Workday (with AI modules)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Greenhouse (with integrations)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SmartRecruiters (with integrations)\\\\\\\"],\\\\n\\\\\\\"market_analysis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The market for AI-powered recruitment solutions is experiencing significant growth, driven by the increasing volume of job applications, the need for efficiency in hiring, and the desire to reduce bias. Companies are actively seeking tools to automate repetitive tasks like initial resume screening, allowing recruiters to focus on high-value activities. There's a strong demand for solutions that can accurately match candidates to job requirements, extract key skills, and provide data-driven insights to accelerate time-to-hire and improve candidate quality. The global HR tech market is expanding, with AI/ML being a key innovation driver, indicating a robust and receptive market for such a platform.\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"target_audience\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Human Resources departments, Talent Acquisition teams, Recruiters (corporate and agency), Staffing firms, Hiring Managers, Enterprise-level organizations with high volume hiring needs, Small to Medium Businesses (SMBs) looking to optimize their recruitment process without large internal teams.\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"monetization\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"Subscription-based tiers (e.g., Basic, Pro, Enterprise) based on features, number of users, or volume of resumes processed per month/year.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Per-resume processing fee for ad-hoc usage or overage charges.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Custom enterprise solutions with dedicated support and integrations.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Value-added services such as advanced analytics, bias detection reports, or integration with existing ATS/HRIS systems.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Freemium model with limited features or resume processing capacity, encouraging upgrade to paid tiers.\\\\\\\"],\\\\n\\\\\\\"technical_risks\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"Accuracy and bias in AI/ML models: Ensuring the models accurately parse resumes, extract relevant information, and match candidates without introducing or amplifying existing biases (e.g., gender, race, age). Requires extensive training data and continuous monitoring.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Data quality and volume for AI training: Obtaining sufficient, diverse, and high-quality resume and job description data to train robust and generalizable AI models.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Scalability of AI inference: Processing a large volume of resumes in real-time or near real-time as the user base grows.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Integration complexity: Seamlessly integrating with various Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS) and Human Resources Information Systems (HRIS) used by clients.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Security and privacy of sensitive candidate data: Protecting personal information on resumes and ensuring compliance with regulations like GDPR, CCPA.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Performance of NLP models: Ensuring efficient and accurate parsing of diverse resume formats and unstructured text.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Infrastructure cost management for AI/ML operations.\\\\\\\"],\\\\n\\\\\\\"business_risks\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"Market competition: Facing established players and new startups in the HR tech space.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Data privacy and compliance: Navigating complex and evolving data privacy regulations globally (GDPR, CCPA, etc.) and building trust with users regarding sensitive candidate data.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Client adoption and change management: Convincing HR teams to adopt new technology and integrate it into their existing workflows.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Perception of 'AI replacing humans': Overcoming resistance from recruiters who might view AI as a threat rather than an assistant.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Bias accusations: Potential for negative publicity or legal challenges if the AI is perceived to be biased in its screening.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Pricing strategy: Finding the right balance to attract customers while ensuring profitability.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Reliance on third-party integrations: Dependence on APIs and data formats of other HR systems.\\\\\\\"],\\\\n\\\\\\\"mvp_features\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"User authentication and authorization (recruiter/admin roles).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Job description parsing and creation (manual input or upload).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Resume upload functionality (single and bulk).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Basic resume parsing and key information extraction (skills, experience, education).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"AI-powered matching of resumes to job descriptions with a relevance score.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Candidate ranking based on matching score.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Simple candidate profile view with extracted information.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Search and filter capabilities for screened candidates.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Dashboard for recruiters to view active jobs and candidate pipelines.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Feedback mechanism for AI model improvement (e.g., 'thumbs up/down' on matches).\\\\\\\"]}\\\"}\"],\"options\":{\"google_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"]},\"base_url\":\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com\",\"model\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\",\"temperature\":0.2},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"{\\\"architecture_type\\\":\\\"Microservices Architecture\\\",\\n\\\"frontend_architecture\\\":\\\"React.js with Next.js for server-side rendering and routing, leveraging a component-based design system (e.g., Material-UI, Ant Design) for consistent UI/UX.\\\",\\n\\\"backend_architecture\\\":\\\"Polyglot Microservices: Core services (Auth, User, Job, Candidate) implemented using Node.js with Express/NestJS for high I/O performance. AI/ML-intensive services (Resume Processing, AI Matching) implemented using Python with FastAPI for efficient data processing and integration with ML libraries. Services communicate via RESTful APIs and asynchronous message queues.\\\",\\n\\\"database_design\\\":\\\"PostgreSQL: Primary relational database for structured data such as user accounts, job descriptions, candidate metadata (name, contact, status), and system configurations. MongoDB (or similar Document Database): For storing raw uploaded resumes and their parsed, unstructured/semi-structured JSON representations, offering schema flexibility. Redis: In-memory data store for caching frequently accessed data, session management, and as a message broker for certain asynchronous tasks.\\\",\\n\\\"api_design\\\":[\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Auth Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/auth/register\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/login\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/refresh-token\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/logout\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Handles user registration, authentication, and token management (JWT).\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"User Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"GET /api/users/{id}\\\",\\\"PUT /api/users/{id}\\\",\\\"GET /api/users/profile\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages user profiles, roles, and permissions.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Job Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/jobs\\\",\\\"GET /api/jobs\\\",\\\"GET /api/jobs/{id}\\\",\\\"PUT /api/jobs/{id}\\\",\\\"DELETE /api/jobs/{id}\\\",\\\"GET /api/jobs/{id}/candidates\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages job postings, including creation, retrieval, update, and deletion. Provides endpoints to view candidates associated with a job.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Resume Processing Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/resumes/upload\\\",\\\"GET /api/resumes/{id}/parsed-data\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Handles resume file uploads, triggers asynchronous parsing, and provides access to parsed resume data. (Internal endpoint for parsing triggered by upload).\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"AI Matching Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/jobs/{jobId}/match\\\",\\\"POST /api/candidates/{candidateId}/feedback\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Triggers AI-powered matching of candidates to a specific job, returning ranked results. Accepts feedback for model improvement.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Candidate Service API\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"GET /api/candidates\\\",\\\"GET /api/candidates/{id}\\\",\\\"PUT /api/candidates/{id}\\\",\\\"DELETE /api/candidates/{id}\\\",\\\"GET /api/candidates/search\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages candidate profiles, including search, filtering, and detailed views of extracted information.\\\"}\\n],\\n\\\"folder_structure\\\":[\\n\\\"./frontend/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/auth-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/user-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/job-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/resume-processing-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/ai-matching-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./services/candidate-service/\\\",\\n\\\"./shared/\\\",\\n\\\"./infrastructure/\\\",\\n\\\"./docs/\\\"\\n],\\n\\\"microservices\\\":[\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Auth Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages user authentication, registration, login, and JWT token issuance/validation.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"User Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Handles user profiles, roles (recruiter, admin), and permissions.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Job Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages job postings, job description parsing, and associated metadata.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Resume Processing Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Responsible for handling resume uploads, extracting text, and parsing key information (skills, experience, education) using NLP techniques. Publishes events to a message queue upon successful parsing.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"AI Matching Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Consumes parsed job descriptions and resumes, applies AI/ML models to calculate relevance scores, ranks candidates, and stores matching results. Incorporates feedback for continuous model improvement.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Candidate Service\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Manages candidate profiles, provides search and filtering capabilities, and aggregates data from parsed resumes and matching results.\\\"},\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"API Gateway\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Acts as a single entry point for all client requests, handling request routing, authentication enforcement, rate limiting, and potentially caching.\\\"}\\n],\\n\\\"authentication\\\":\\\"JWT (JSON Web Tokens) for stateless authentication. Upon successful login, the Auth Service issues a JWT. This token is then included in subsequent requests to other microservices via the API Gateway, which validates the token's authenticity and authorization before routing the request.\\\",\\n\\\"deployment_architecture\\\":\\\"Cloud-native deployment on AWS (or similar cloud provider like GCP/Azure). Services are containerized using Docker. Kubernetes (EKS) is used for container orchestration, auto-scaling, and high availability. An API Gateway (e.g., AWS API Gateway) handles request routing, load balancing, and initial authentication. AWS S3 is used for storing raw uploaded resumes. AWS SQS/Kafka is used for asynchronous communication between microservices (e.g., triggering resume parsing after upload, triggering AI matching). CI/CD pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) automate builds, tests, and deployments.\\\",\\n\\\"scalability_plan\\\":\\\"Horizontal Scaling: All microservices are designed to be stateless and can be scaled independently based on demand using Kubernetes auto-scaling. Asynchronous Processing: Heavy tasks like resume parsing and AI matching are handled asynchronously via message queues (AWS SQS/Kafka) to decouple operations and prevent blocking the main request flow. Caching: Redis is used for caching frequently accessed data (e.g., job descriptions, user sessions) to reduce database load. Database Scaling: PostgreSQL can be scaled with read replicas for read-heavy workloads and potentially sharding for extreme write loads. MongoDB inherently supports horizontal scaling. CDN: A Content Delivery Network (CDN) is used for serving static frontend assets to improve load times and reduce latency.\\\",\\n\\\"security_considerations\\\":[\\n\\\"Data Encryption: All data is encrypted at rest (database, S3 storage) and in transit (TLS/SSL for all internal and external communication).\\\",\\n\\\"Access Control: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is implemented to ensure users (recruiters, admins) only access resources and perform actions aligned with their permissions.\\\",\\n\\\"Input Validation: Strict input validation is applied at the API Gateway and within each microservice to prevent common vulnerabilities like injection attacks (SQL, XSS).\\\",\\n\\\"Secure API Gateway: The API Gateway enforces authentication, authorization, rate limiting, and acts as a Web Application Firewall (WAF) to protect against common web exploits.\\\",\\n\\\"Secrets Management: Sensitive credentials (database passwords, API keys) are stored and managed securely using a dedicated secrets management service (e.g., AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault).\\\",\\n\\\"Compliance: Design and implement data handling practices to comply with relevant data privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) for sensitive candidate information. Data anonymization/pseudonymization is considered where feasible.\\\",\\n\\\"Bias Mitigation in AI: Continuous monitoring, auditing, and retraining of AI models to detect and mitigate algorithmic bias in candidate matching and ranking. Explainable AI (XAI) techniques are explored to provide transparency.\\\",\\n\\\"Least Privilege: All services and users are granted only the minimum necessary permissions to perform their functions.\\\",\\n\\\"Regular Security Audits: Periodic penetration testing, vulnerability scanning, and code reviews are conducted to identify and address security weaknesses.\\\"\\n]\\n}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":1587,\"promptTokens\":1081,\"totalTokens\":2668}}}"}}
